      ":question/id": "fa9a90c8-68ec-5392-a3c8-0ae9ab63850c",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-158202",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}(y-2x)?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\ny-2x>0\\,\\Longrightarrow\\,y>2x\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y>2x\\}.\n$$\n\nSince the expression involves the $>$ sign, the line is *not* part of the domain. Therefore, we draw the dashed line $y=2x$ and shade the region *above* the line.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](images/42/42e2faf3df63b038b57d2fddc9b7ef2c2e720dae6e0a8524d602b7ac93681b3d.png)"
    },
